{"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Error Presentation","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default Error placeholders do beyond showing a generic icon and message: telling a connectivity problem apart from everything else, an optional second action alongside Retry, and a user-facing message distinct from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/errorpresentation"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ErrorPresentation"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the one state whose presentation can’t be fully generic — a timed-out request, a missing article, and a malformed response all deserve different words, and sometimes a different action, even though they’re all just an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference"},{"text":". This article rounds up the three pieces ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","type":"reference"},{"text":" use to narrow that gap without you writing a fully custom placeholder.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-offline-aware-variant","text":"The offline-aware variant"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/isConnectivityError(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" indicating no network connectivity (","type":"text"},{"code":".notConnectedToInternet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".networkConnectionLost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or a timed-out request (","type":"text"},{"code":".timedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). When it’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the default Error placeholders swap their usual warning-triangle icon and “Something Went Wrong” title for a ","type":"text"},{"code":"wifi.exclamationmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" icon and “Connection Issue” instead — the same distinction a fully custom placeholder can make with the same check:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["if ScreenState<Never>.isConnectivityError(error) {","    \/\/ show your own offline-specific treatment","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other error, including other ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" codes, falls back to the generic treatment.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-secondary-action-slot","text":"The secondary action slot"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both default Error placeholders take an optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"secondaryAction: (title: String, action: () -> Void)?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alongside ","type":"text"},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a second button for something other than retrying, like going back to the previous screen instead of hammering a request that’s going to fail the same way again:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateDefaultErrorView(error: error, onRetry: reload, secondaryAction: (title: \"Go Back\", action: goBack))","ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView(error: error, onRetry: reload, secondaryAction: (title: \"Go Back\", action: goBack))"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default, so every existing call site keeps showing just Retry (or nothing, if ","type":"text"},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is also ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") until you opt in.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"A-user-facing-message-distinct-from-localizedDescription","text":"A user-facing message, distinct from localizedDescription"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"error.localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is often a debugging string, or — for a plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomStringConvertible","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"LocalizedError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance — just the type name, not something to put in front of the person using the app. Conform your own error type to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","type":"reference"},{"text":" to supply a message meant to actually be read:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct APIError: ScreenStateDisplayableError {","    let displayMessage: String","}","","store.setError(APIError(displayMessage: \"That article was removed.\"))"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/displayMessage(for:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" checks for that conformance and falls back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for every other error. The default Error placeholders call it instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"error.localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly, so adopting ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","type":"reference"},{"text":" is enough to change what they show — no call-site changes needed.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"]},{"anchor":"Error-presentation","title":"Error presentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError"],"generated":true}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/displayMessage(for:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/displaymessage(for:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/displayMessage(for:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The message to show for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":": its "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError\/displayMessage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when it conforms to that protocol, otherwise "